     "text": "```python\nfrom typing import List, Tuple\n\ndef average_diagonal(matrix: List[List[float]]) -> float:\n    \"\"\"\n    Computes the average of the diagonal elements of a given square matrix.\n\n    Args:\n        matrix: A square matrix represented as a list of lists of floats.\n\n    Returns:\n        The average of the diagonal elements.\n\n    Raises:\n        ValueError: If the matrix is not square (i.e., the number of rows is not equal to the number of columns).\n    \"\"\"\n    if not matrix:\n        raise ValueError(\"The matrix cannot be empty.\")\n    \n    rows = len(matrix)\n    cols = len(matrix[0])\n    \n    if rows != cols:\n        raise ValueError(\"The matrix must be square (number of rows must equal the number of columns).\")\n    \n    diagonal_sum = 0.0\n    for i in range(rows):\n        diagonal_sum += matrix[i][i]\n    \n    return diagonal_sum / rows\n```",
